# Read automatically by Vite during `npm run build` (production mode). No build ARG, no platform
# variable — the value is baked into the bundle from this file.
#
# Why this exists: Railway would not surface its VITE_API_BASE_URL service variable to the Docker
# build (the bundle kept shipping an empty base URL), and its private DNS (*.railway.internal)
# never resolved from the frontend container, so nginx cannot proxy /api. The SPA therefore calls
# the backend's PUBLIC domain directly. That makes the API cross-origin, which is why the backend
# needs APP_AUTH_COOKIE_SAME_SITE=None and the frontend origin in APP_CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS.
#
# This is not a secret — it is a public hostname that ships in the JS bundle either way.
#
# !! REPLACE with your backend service's public Railway domain. No trailing slash. !!
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://REPLACE-ME-backend.up.railway.app
